# wall_panel: an e-ink panel device as a remote framebuffer; the server draws, the device only applies blits and returns touches.
# Live path: paneld (C, on the device) + panel-server (Rust, on the server host) + chrome-headless-shell + HTML pages.
# Outside the live path (legacy): panel/, srv/, device/.

# --- machines
The program "wall_panel" contains the process "paneld", the process "panel-server", the process "chrome-headless-shell", the process "mosquitto", the process "curl", the shell script "deploy.sh" and the directory "pages".
The process "paneld" runs on the machine "panel device".
The process "panel-server" runs on the machine "server host".
The process "chrome-headless-shell" runs on the machine "server host".
The process "mosquitto" runs on the machine "server host".
The process "curl" runs on the machine "server host".
The shell script "deploy.sh" runs on the machine "dev workstation".
The process "paneld" runs in the execution context "init session".
The process "panel-server" runs in the execution context "systemd panel-server.service".
The process "chrome-headless-shell" runs in the execution context "systemd, Nice 19".

# --- inside each process
The process "paneld" contains the state machine "screen ownership", the device "EPDC framebuffer", the device "digitizer", the list "touch targets" and the timer "reconnect backoff".
The process "panel-server" contains the thread "accept device", the thread "session ping", the thread "control", the thread "monitor", the thread "mqtt", the thread "weather", the thread "clock", the key-value store "Store", the queue "alert queue", the stack "navigation stack", the map "screen cache" and the configuration "config.json".
The directory "pages" contains the page "home.html", the page "launcher.html" and the page "dark theme".

# --- endpoints and connections
The process "panel-server" listens on the tcp endpoint "server:8993".
The process "panel-server" listens on the http endpoint "server:9000".
The process "chrome-headless-shell" listens on the devtools endpoint "0.0.0.0:9222".
The process "mosquitto" listens on the mqtt endpoint "127.0.0.1:1883".
The process "paneld" connects to the tcp endpoint "server:8993".
# the device protocol does not authenticate: the local network is the boundary
The tcp endpoint "server:8993" needs no authentication.
The process "panel-server" connects to the devtools endpoint "0.0.0.0:9222".
The thread "mqtt" connects to the mqtt endpoint "127.0.0.1:1883".
The thread "mqtt" subscribes to the value "home/energy/#", the value "home/weather/#" and the value "home/sensor/data".
The thread "weather" launches the process "curl".
The process "curl" reads the value "forecast" from the web service "open-meteo".
The process "panel-server" sends the message "BLIT" to the process "paneld".
The process "paneld" sends the message "TOUCH" to the process "panel-server".
The process "panel-server" sends the message "CMD launch app" to the process "paneld".
The process "panel-server" renders the page "home.html" into the device "buffer L8 1072x1448".
The process "panel-server" uses the process "chrome-headless-shell".
The process "panel-server" reads the page "home.html" from the directory "pages".
The process "panel-server" reads the configuration "config.json".
The shell script "deploy.sh" writes the process "panel-server" to the machine "server host".
The shell script "deploy.sh" writes the directory "pages" to the machine "server host".

# --- threads and what they share
The thread "mqtt" fills the key-value store "Store".
The thread "weather" fills the key-value store "Store".
The thread "clock" fills the key-value store "Store".
The thread "accept device" consumes the key-value store "Store".
The thread "accept device" consumes the queue "alert queue".
The thread "monitor" consumes the key-value store "Store".
The thread "monitor" fills the queue "alert queue".
The thread "control" fills the queue "alert queue".
The thread "accept device" changes the map "screen cache".
The thread "accept device" changes the stack "navigation stack".
The thread "session ping" repeats every "5 s".
The thread "clock" repeats every "60 s".
The thread "weather" repeats every "1800 s".
The key-value store "Store" is keyed by the value "data key".
The map "screen cache" is keyed by the value "page".
The queue "alert queue" is bounded.
The timer "reconnect backoff" repeats every "1 s to 60 s".

# --- state machines
The state machine "screen ownership" has the states "session" and "external app".
The state machine "screen ownership" starts in the state "session".
The process "paneld" moves the state machine "screen ownership" from the state "session" to the state "external app".
The process "paneld" moves the state machine "screen ownership" from the state "external app" to the state "session".
The process "panel-server" contains the state machine "SOC alert".
The state machine "SOC alert" has the states "normal" and "alert".
The state machine "SOC alert" starts in the state "normal".
The thread "monitor" moves the state machine "SOC alert" from the state "normal" to the state "alert".
The thread "monitor" moves the state machine "SOC alert" from the state "alert" to the state "normal".
The process "paneld" contains the state machine "connection".
The state machine "connection" has the states "disconnected", "connected" and "waiting backoff".
The state machine "connection" starts in the state "disconnected".
The process "paneld" moves the state machine "connection" from the state "disconnected" to the state "connected".
The process "paneld" moves the state machine "connection" from the state "connected" to the state "waiting backoff".
The process "paneld" moves the state machine "connection" from the state "waiting backoff" to the state "disconnected".

# --- invariants: e-ink
The process "paneld" never calls the function "FB_WAIT_UPDATE".
The process "panel-server" never changes the value "physical screen edge".
If the value "rectangle" is monochrome, the process "panel-server" uses the value "A2".
If the stack "navigation stack" changes, the process "panel-server" uses the value "GC16".
If the counter "consecutive A2 per region" is at least 8, the process "panel-server" dispatches the event "ghosting cleanup".
The process "paneld" resolves the list "touch targets".

# --- invariants: resilience
If the devtools endpoint "0.0.0.0:9222" times out, the process "panel-server" falls back to the function "native render".
If the connection "session" closes, the process "paneld" connects to the tcp endpoint "server:8993".
If the connection "session" times out, the process "paneld" launches the process "udhcpc".
The connection "session" times out after "30 s".
If the value "home.soc" is less than 30, the thread "monitor" publishes the alert "low SOC" to the queue "alert queue".
If the value "home.soc" is greater than 35, the thread "monitor" removes the alert "low SOC" from the queue "alert queue".
If the thread "mqtt" times out, the thread "monitor" publishes the alert "dead source" to the queue "alert queue".
The configuration "config.json" is immutable.
The process "panel-server" validates the configuration "config.json".
The shell script "deploy.sh" never overwrites the configuration "config.json".
When the process "chrome-headless-shell" starts, the process "chrome-headless-shell" removes the value "SingletonLock".
